Classic Github 0.1Your code. Your Macintosh.This installer places Classic Github, its login helper and documentationin the Classic Github folder. Keep the two applications together.The login helper starts automatically when it is needed; it is not aStartup Item. Your GitHub password is never entered on the Macintosh.FIRST LAUNCH1. Open Classic Github. Choose Help > Secure Networking Setup.2. Smash the keyboard and move the mouse inside the setup window.   Vary your keys, direction and pace. Allow at least 30 seconds.3. Continue when the button lights up. Choose a local vault passphrase.4. Choose Help > Test GitHub Connection.5. Sign in from File > Preferences. Approve the code on your phone   or a modern computer at https://github.com/login/device.The local vault passphrase is separate from your GitHub password.Creating or unlocking the vault can take a while. Saved setup is reused.Each Macintosh creates its own network state and saved login.SYSTEM AND MEMORYSystem 7.5.3 or later with Open Transport is the target. The release istested in QEMU with Mac OS 9.2.2. Physical 68040 testing remains open.The application is FAT 68K/PowerPC and is designed for 640x480 displays.Preferred application memory is 192 MB, with an 8 MB minimum. Largerrepositories need the preferred allocation. Quit before changing memoryin Finder Get Info. Fetch bodies are limited to 64 MiB, expanded packsto 64 MiB, outgoing packs to 128 MiB on disk, and individual Git objects to 2 MiB.SOURCE AND NOTICEShttps://github.com/bbenchoff/GitHubClassicIndependent software. Third-party notices are included in LICENSES.txt.